<header><h1>Warfare (Strategy Card): Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_warfare">Warfare (Strategy Card)</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Rules Reference</h2>
    <ul>
    <li>To resolve the primary ability on the <i>Warfare</i> strategy card, the active player performs the following:<sup>13</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>13</sup> Warfare (Thunder&rsquo;s Edge), primary: &ldquo;Perform a tactical action in any system without placing a command token, even if the system already has your command token in it; that system still counts as being activated. You may redistribute your command tokens before and after this action.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The active player performs a tactical action in any system without placing a command token, even if the system already has their command token in it; that system still counts as being activated.<sup>2,13</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>13</sup> Warfare (Thunder&rsquo;s Edge), primary: &ldquo;Perform a tactical action in any system without placing a command token, even if the system already has your command token in it; that system still counts as being activated.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Warfare strategy card work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The primary lets you redistribute your tokens and perform a tactical action without placing a command token, even in a system that already holds yours or a Diplomacy token &hellip; that system still counts as activated.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The active player may redistribute their command tokens before and after this tactical action.<sup>2,13</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>13</sup> Warfare (Thunder&rsquo;s Edge), primary: &ldquo;You may redistribute your command tokens before and after this action.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Warfare strategy card work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The primary lets you redistribute your tokens and perform a tactical action without placing a command token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After the active player resolves the primary ability of the <i>Warfare</i> strategy card, each other player, beginning with the player to the left of the active player and proceeding clockwise, may spend one command token from their strategy pool to resolve the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> abilities of units in their home system.<sup>2,13</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>13</sup> Warfare (Thunder&rsquo;s Edge), secondary: &ldquo;Spend 1 token from your Strategy Pool to use the PRODUCTION abilities of units in your home system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Warfare strategy card work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The secondary produces with all your units in your home system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ul>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Resolving the secondary ability of Warfare does not activate the player&rsquo;s home system. It may be resolved even if that system already contains one of their command tokens.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Warfare secondary work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It doesn&rsquo;t activate the system and works even if your home system already has your token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a tactical action that is part of the <i>Warfare</i> primary ability is canceled, or the resolving player&rsquo;s turn is ended, the rest of the strategy card is still resolved.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;If a tactical action that is part of the Warfare primary is canceled, or the resolving player&rsquo;s turn is ended, the rest of the strategy card is still resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During the tactical action of the <i>Warfare</i> primary ability, ships may move into a system that contains one of the player&rsquo;s command tokens, but ships still cannot move out of a system that contains one of the player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Warfare strategy card work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You can move ships into an already-activated system that way, but not out of one.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>No command token is placed in the system where the <i>Warfare</i> primary ability is resolved, so ships in that system, including ones produced there, may move during a later tactical action that round.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Warfare strategy card work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;perform a tactical action without placing a command token, even in a system that already holds yours or a Diplomacy token, so newly produced ships can move later that round; that system still counts as activated.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>
</article>
